      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic non-traumatic heel pain is not an uncommon symptom in patients presenting to GP, orthopaedic or rheumatological clinics. A full history and examination will provide a diagnosis in most cases. Rarer causes need to be excluded in certain patients. This article outlines the differential diagnosis and discusses the more common causes."},
